Reason:
The `destroy_linker` function was called in a loop that iterated through all linkers, which resulted in the removal of all linkers associated with the dialog instead of just the specific one intended. This improper handling caused memory leaks and incorrect state management, as the actual linker that `unset_dlg_profile` was meant to remove was not being handled correctly.

